{"strongs": "H5046", "word": "נָגַד", "translit": "na.gad", "root": "נגד", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "be conspicuous", "definition": "[ נָגַד ] 363 verb be conspicuous (Late Hebrew in derivatives; Phoenician proper name, masculine נגד ; Arabic conquer, overcome , also be apparent, conspicuous ; high land or country ; be courageous, vigorous, effective , courageous, efficient ; Aramaic , נְגַד drag, draw, lead ; נָגוֺדָא leader ; Ethiopic is travel ); — Hiph`il 328 Perfect הִגִּיד Gen 3:11 +, 3 feminine singular הִגִּ֫ידָה 1Sam 25:19 +, הִגַּדְתָּ Gen 12:8 +, etc.; Imperfect יַגִּיד 1Sam 9:6 +; וַיַּגֵּד Gen 9:22 +; suffix יַגִּידֶ֫הָ Isa 44:7 יַגִּדָהּ Jer 9:11 יַגֵָּֽדְךָ Deut 32:7 (jussive), etc.; Imperative הַגֵּד 2Sam 18:21 +; הַגִּ֫ידָה Gen 29:15 +, etc.; Infinitive absolute הַגֵּד Judg 14:12 + 2 t.; הַגֵּיד Jer 36:16 construct לְהַגִּיד Gen 32:6 +; לגיד 2Kgs 9:15 Kt . ( Qr ׳ לְהַגּ ); Participle מַגִּיד Gen 41:24 +; feminine מַגֶּ֫דֶת Esth 2:20 plural construct מַגִּידֵי Judg 14:19 — declare, tell [usually followed by לְ of indirect object Gen 3:11 + often; insert also 1Sam 12:7 ; 2Sam 13:34 ᵐ5 Th We Klo Dr Kit Bu , so HPS 2Sam 13:34 ( 1Sam 12:7 he following HCT as more different); followed by אֶל Exod 19:9 ; 1Sam 3:15 followed by לִפְנֵי 1Sam 17:31 ; Ps 142:3 עַלפָּֿנָיו Job 21:31 בְּאָזְנֵָי Jer 36:20 followed by בְּ local (instead of indirect object) chiefly prophets Jer 4:5 ; Jer 5:20 ; Jer 31:10 +; also 1Sam 4:13 ; 2Sam 1:20 ; 2Kgs 9:15 ; Mic 1:10 rarely followed by accusative of person 2Sam 15:31 (but read וּלְדָוִד הִגִּיד HPS (indefinite subject), or הֻגַּד ׳ ולס We Dr Kit , ᵐ5 ᵑ9 Th Klo Bu favour הֻגַּד ), 2Kgs 7:9 ; 2Kgs 7:11 ; Ezek 43:10 ; Job 17:5 ; Job 26:4 ; Job 31:37 followed by direct object in accusative Gen 45:13 + often; followed by clause with כִּי Gen 3:11 + often; followed by clause with אֲשֶׁר = כִּי (late) Esth 3:4 ; Esth 6:2 followed by clause with מָה Gen 29:15 ; Judg 16:15 ; Esth 8:1 +; followed by clause with מִי 2Kgs 6:11 followed by clause with אֵיבָה Song 1:7 , once followed by clause with הֲ Gen 43:6 , etc.; often no direct object, followed by לֵאמֹר Exod 13:8 ; 1Sam 25:14 +; followed by וַיּאֹמֶר Gen 47:1 +; אמר then following by oratio recta [direct speech]; ׳ הִגּ alone followed by oratio recta Zech 9:12 followed by עַל concerning , 1Sam 27:11 ; Esth 6:2 often indirect object omitted 1Sam 24:19 +; direct object omitted Judg 13:10 +; both omitted Lev 5:1 + ]. In Hexateuch rarely P , Lev 5:1 ; Lev 14:35 ; Exod 16:22 ; J , Gen 3:11 ; Gen 12:18 ; Exod 13:8 + 18 t.; E , Gen 21:6 ; Gen 31:20 ; Gen 41:25 + 15 t.; D , Deut 17:9 ; Deut 26:3 ; Deut 30:18 + 5 t.; — 1. tell, announce, report , usually human subject Gen 9:22 ; Gen 24:23 ; Gen 32:6 ; Lev 14:35 ; Judg 13:6 ; 1Sam 3:18 ; 1Kgs 1:23 ; Neh 2:12 ; Esth 2:10 (twice in verse); Job 12:7 ; Ps 142:3 ; Isa 19:12 ; Jer 5:20 ; Ezek 24:19 +. 2. declare, make known, expound , especially of something before not understood, concealed or mysterious, Gen 3:11 ; Gen 12:18 , etc.; 1Kgs 10:3 = 2Chr 9:2 a riddle Judg 14:12 ; Judg 14:15 ; Judg 14:16 (3 t. in verse); Judg 14:19 dream Dan 2:2 secret Job 11:6 , etc.; of ׳ י as revealing, Gen 41:25 ; 2Sam 7:11 ; 2Kgs 4:27 ; Mic 6:8 ; Jer 42:3 ; Ps 147:19 of declaring by ׳ י 's agents Deut 5:5 ; Mic 3:8 ; 1Sam 15:16 ; 2Sam 24:13 ; Jer 50:28 ; Isa 58:1 by divin. Hos 4:12 . 3. inform of (play the informer concerning) Josh 2:14 ; Josh 2:20 ; Jer 20:10 ; Job 17:5 ; Lev 5:1 ; Prov 29:24 . 4. publish declare, proclaim , especially of proclaiming wisdom, power, loving-kindness, etc., of ׳ י (especially Psalms): Ps 9:12 ; Ps 22:32 ; Ps 51:17 ; Ps 92:3 ; Ps 92:16 ; Ps 145:4 +, subject heavens Ps 19:2 ; Ps 50:6 ; Ps 97:6 ; Isa 42:12 ; Isa 57:12 . 5. avow, acknowledge, confess: Isa 3:9 ; Ps 38:19 , compare Isa 48:6 . — Participle = messenger 2Sam 15:13 ; Jer 51:31 (twice in verse) compare הַנַּ֫עַר הַמַּגִּיד 2Sam 1:5 ; 2Sam 1:6 ; 2Sam 1:13 ׳ הָאִישׁ הַמּ 2Sam 18:11 . Hoph`al Perfect הֻגַּד Josh 9:24 +; Imperfect וַיֻּגַּד Gen 22:20 +; Infinitive absolute הֻגֵּד Josh 9:24 ; Ruth 2:11 — be told, announced, reported , always followed by לְ (sometimes impersonal, logical subject in accusative, compare Gen 27:42 ; 2Sam 21:11 , with feminine Isa 21:2 not in P ): Gen 27:42 ( J ), Gen 31:22 ( E ), Deut 17:4 ; Josh 9:24 (twice in verse) ( D ), Ruth 2:11 (twice in verse); Judg 9:25 ; 2Sam 10:17 ; 2Sam 19:2 ; 2Sam 21:11 ; 2Sam 1:7 ; 2Sam 18:13 ; 2Sam 1:17 ; 2Sam 2:6 ; 2Sam 40:21 followed by לֵאמֹר Gen 22:20 ; Gen 38:13 ; Gen 13:24 (all J ), Josh 10:17 ( J E ), 1Sam 15:12 ; 1Sam 19:19 ; 2Sam 6:12 ; 1Kgs 1:51 ; 2Kgs 6:13 ; 2Kgs 8:7 ; Isa 7:2 followed by clause with כִּי Exod 14:5 ( J ), Judg 9:47 ; Judg 1:7 ; Judg 23:13 ; Judg 27:4 ; Judg 1:29 ; Judg 29:41 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4962')\">BDB4962</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5046')\">H5046</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4961')\">BDB4961</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4963')\">BDB4963</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>נָגַד</bdbheb>]<sub>363</sub> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>be conspicuous</highlightword> (Late Hebrew in derivatives; Phoenician proper name, masculine <bdbheb>נגד</bdbheb>; Arabic <placeholder3160/> <highlight>conquer, overcome</highlight>, also <highlight>be apparent, conspicuous</highlight>; <placeholder3161/> <highlight>high land</highlight> or <highlight>country</highlight>; <placeholder3162/> <highlight>be courageous, vigorous, effective</highlight>, <placeholder3163/> <highlight>courageous, efficient</highlight>; Aramaic <placeholder3164/>, <bdbheb>נְגַד</bdbheb> <highlight>drag, draw, lead</highlight>; <placeholder3165/> <bdbheb>נָגוֺדָא</bdbheb> <highlight>leader</highlight>; Ethiopic <placeholder3166/> is <highlight>travel</highlight>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>Hiph`il</b><sub>328</sub> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> <bdbheb>הִגִּיד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 3:11\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick